 Build the Future with Us 
 Are you driven by cybersecurity, proactive risk management, and creating sustainable value, and eager to contribute to the purpose of a company that aims to help its clients feel confident and secure about their future? As an Information Security Advisor, you will play a key role in supporting IT delivery teams and business partners in the secure delivery of technology solutions while managing risks in a pragmatic manner aligned with business realities.
 This position is a great opportunity to showcase your skills and fully realize your potential within a caring and trustworthy company. Here, people and their development are at the heart of our priorities, fostering an environment that encourages collaboration and innovation.
 What You'll Accomplish With Us 
 As an Information security Advisor, you will be at the core of our mission. Here are the main responsibilities:
 Advise IT delivery teams and business partners on integrating security requirements and risk management best practices;
 Provide consulting support throughout the design, implementation, operation, and evolution phases of technology solutions;
 Assess risks related to technology solutions, data, and business processes;
 Develop pragmatic, actionable recommendations tailored to various technological and business contexts;
 Actively contribute to the continuous improvement of the organization's cybersecurity posture and the maturity of its teams;
 Act as a trusted partner to technical and business stakeholders.
 What Could Accelerate Your Success in This Role 
 We are looking for someone who:
 Is recognized for their advanced expertise in information security, technology, and risk management;
 Stands out for their ability to influence, simplify complex concepts, and provide advisory services without formal authority;
 Demonstrates strong rigor, objectivity, and autonomy in analysis and assessments;
 Is recognized for their expert leadership and ability to collaborate effectively with multidisciplinary teams;
 Has a minimum of 7 years of relevant experience in information security, technology, or risk management;
 Holds a bachelor's degree in information technology, information security, data science, or an equivalent field;
 Has strong knowledge of information security frameworks, principles, and practices;
 Holds a CISSP, CCSP, or CRISC certification, considered an asset;
 Demonstrates flexibility, comfort with ambiguity, and a commitment to continuous learning;
 Has strong relationship-building skills with vendors and external partners;
 Has experience with or an interest in using artificial intelligence tools (e.g., Copilot, Generative AI) to support analysis, writing, or process optimization, considered an asset;
 Has knowledge of the insurance and financial services industry, considered an asset;
 Has an advanced level of proficiency in both French and English, as the incumbent will be required to communicate daily with English-speaking vendors across Canada through emails and phone calls.
